wt/external/wpt/css/css-writing-modes/sizing-percentages-replaced-orthogonal-001*.html
#
# The selection colors. LookAndFeel::ColorID::Highlight and Highlighttext are
# the desktop's on both sides: widget/gtk/nsLookAndFeel.cpp reads them off the
# GTK selection style context, widget/windows/nsLookAndFeel.cpp answers with
# GetSysColor(COLOR_HIGHLIGHT) and COLOR_HIGHLIGHTTEXT. Here that is #3daee9
# under #fcfcfc, there #0078d4 under #ffffff, and nsXPLookAndFeel's own
# #3399ff stands behind neither, so no font decision reaches these pixels.
# Pinning both sides with `::selection { background-color: #808080; color:
# #000 }` makes every cell below that colors through that pseudo-element
# identical, which says the text under the highlight matches byte for byte.
# The four that stay are the same two colors reached another way: the
# Highlight and HighlightText CSS keywords, the caret, and an SVG fill the
# pseudo-element does not cover.
wt/external/wpt/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-color-selection-002.html
