#
# The text caret. These four pages call focus() on an editable element on load,
# and Gecko draws a caret in the element that has it. Here every browser owns
# an Xvfb screen and its window is the active one, so the caret is painted; on
# the guest no browser window is active when wincap photographs it, so none of
# them paints one, the same way on all eight ports. Each cell differs by the
# same 104 px, a two-pixel column 53 rows tall at the left edge of the control,
# and by nothing else. run_parity_firefox.sh sets ui.caretBlinkTime to 0 on
# both sides so the caret is not a blink phase on top of that.
wt/external/wpt/css/css-pseudo/grammar-spelling-errors-00[12].html
wt/external/wpt/css/css-pseudo/reference/grammar-spelling-errors-00[12]-ref.html
#
# A dashed border, not text. The scroll box these two pages draw carries
# "border: black dashed", and one dash along the top border and one along the
# bottom start half a pixel into column 390. The edge pixel there is 106 on
# Linux and 104 on Windows, a dash phase apart by eight thousandths of a
# pixel, and nothing else in either page differs. A box with the same border,
# width and height and no text on the page reproduces both clusters exactly,
# so no glyph takes part and font metrics cannot reach it.
wt/external/wpt/css/css-text-decor/text-underline-offset-scroll-001.html
wt/external/wpt/css/css-text-decor/reference/text-underline-offset-scroll-001-notref.html
